        "subject": "LU-17000 osd-ldiskfs: widen quota block offsets before shifting",
        "message": "LU-17000 osd-ldiskfs: widen quota block offsets before shifting\n\nThe quota tree walker turns a block number into a file offset with\n\"blk << LUSTRE_DQBLKSIZE_BITS\".  blk is an unsigned int read straight\noff disk with le32_to_cpu(), so the shift is evaluated in 32 bits and\nwraps for any block at or past 4 GiB into the quota file, and the\ntruncated value is then widened to the loff_t it is stored in.\n\nCast blk to loff_t before shifting.  Only the quota_read() offset in\nquota_read_blk() has an observable effect today: a wrapped offset there\nreads a different, live block of the quota file.  The other two sites\nare corrected for consistency but cannot be seen - osd_it_quota::\noiq_offset has had no readers since 8fdb46e476 (\"LU-6617 quota: remove\nquota migration code\"), and find_block_dqentry()'s return value is only\ntested for its sign by osd_it_acct_get(), which the truncation cannot\nchange because the 32-bit product is zero-extended.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 57df6353ca59 (\"LU-1182 ldiskfs-osd: space accounting support\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Iebc7b7decf179362dfd0d15b93955fc89ee6dca4\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68514\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Mikhail Pershin <mpershin@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
